  recipeId: led
  concept: "Authored objective: Safe LED Branch Current.\nAuthored requirement: Verify
    approximately 3-6 mA through the 330 ohm LED resistor. current \u2265 3 mA. current
    \u2264 6 mA. Connection pair R_LED_Input and R_LED_Output.\nGeneral teaching
    principle: An LED has a defined anode and cathode; correct polarity and suitable
    current control matter for normal forward operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Safe LED Branch Current\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Safe LED Branch Current\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 27, perform the objective \u2018Safe LED Branch Current\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Verify approximately
    3-6 mA through the 330 ohm LED resistor. current \u2265 3 mA. current \u2264
    6 mA. Connection pair R_LED_Input and R_LED_Output.\nThe mission evaluator decides
    completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
